WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:16.748
It was raining the next time Aunt Polly attended a Ladies' Aid meeting.

2
00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:23.852
When she came home, her face was flushed, and her hair was damp and windblown.

3
00:00:23.872 --> 00:00:28.914
"Oh, Aunt Polly, you look lovely!

4
00:00:29.715 --> 00:00:31.856
I didn't know your hair curled in the rain."

5
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.801
Aunt Polly tried to smooth her hair.

6
00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:38.801
"No, don't do that!"

7
00:00:39.161 --> 00:00:40.042
Pollyanna cried.

8
00:00:41.122 --> 00:00:44.163
But Aunt Polly had another topic to discuss besides hair.

9
00:00:44.183 --> 00:00:49.464
"Why did you go to the Ladies' Aid meeting to talk about that little beggar boy?

10
00:00:50.705 --> 00:00:53.325
I was so embarrassed when they told me this afternoon!"

11
00:00:53.345 --> 00:01:00.867
"I didn't know the ladies would be more concerned with orphans overseas than Jimmy," Pollyanna burst out.

12
00:01:00.887 --> 00:01:03.088
"Or I would have stayed home.

13
00:01:04.528 --> 00:01:07.169
But I've written to my Ladies' Aid out West about taking him.

14
00:01:08.269 --> 00:01:10.690
So now we'll just have to wait and see what happens."

15
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.551
She paused for a breath.

16
00:01:13.571 --> 00:01:17.412
"Oh, please may I fix your hair like I did Mrs.

17
00:01:17.512 --> 00:01:20.933
Snow's? You'd look so pretty!"

18
00:01:25.274 --> 00:01:28.175
Aunt Polly scolded, but she was secretly pleased.

19
00:01:29.395 --> 00:01:32.756
It had been a long time since anyone had told her that she was pretty.

20
00:01:33.728 --> 00:01:35.549
"You didn't say I couldn't do it!"

21
00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:38.351
Pollyanna cried as she ran for the stairs.

22
00:01:38.371 --> 00:01:40.292
"Let's go upstairs."

23
00:01:40.312 --> 00:01:52.118
"But, Pollyanna, the Ladies' Aid Aunt Polly had that helpless feeling again as she trailed upstairs after her

24
00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:58.921
niece. The next thing Aunt Polly knew, she was sitting at the dressing table in her room.

25
00:02:00.362 --> 00:02:02.443
Pollyanna began styling her hair.

26
00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:10.434
"Turn so you can't see yourself in the mirror," Pollyanna said before leaving the room.

27
00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:15.957
A moment later she returned with a handkerchief that she slipped over Aunt Polly's eyes.

28
00:02:15.977 --> 00:02:17.937
"What are you doing?"

29
00:02:18.418 --> 00:02:19.318
Aunt Polly cried.

30
00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.661
Pollyanna giggled as she pinned a lacy shawl around Aunt Polly's shoulders.

31
00:02:28.222 --> 00:02:31.844
Then she remembered the rosebush that climbed the trellis outside her bedroom window.

32
00:02:33.756 --> 00:02:37.098
Aunt Polly tried to resist as Pollyanna pulled her down the hall.

33
00:02:37.118 --> 00:02:40.539
"Where are you taking me?"

34
00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:41.700
Aunt Polly said.

35
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.441
"You'll see."

36
00:02:46.562 --> 00:02:51.324
Pollyanna leaned out her window and plucked a red rose, which she tucked behind Aunt Polly's ear.

37
00:02:53.605 --> 00:02:56.166
She removed the blindfold and held up a hand mirror.

38
00:02:56.186 --> 00:02:59.428
"Aren't you glad I dressed you up?"

39
00:03:01.664 --> 00:03:04.986
Aunt Polly took in her surroundings and her own reflection.

40
00:03:10.269 --> 00:03:13.151
Then she gave a startled yelp and fled to her room.

41
00:03:15.812 --> 00:03:18.934
At that moment Pollyanna saw a carriage coming up the driveway.

42
00:03:18.954 --> 00:03:21.536
"Dr. Chilton!"

43
00:03:21.916 --> 00:03:23.477
she called with delight from the window.

44
00:03:23.497 --> 00:03:25.538
"Are you looking for me?"

45
00:03:25.558 --> 00:03:28.860
"Yes, will you come outside?"

46
00:03:30.716 --> 00:03:34.879
Rushing into Aunt Polly's room, Pollyanna found her flushed and angry.

47
00:03:36.299 --> 00:03:38.621
Aunt Polly was pulling the pins from the shawl.

48
00:03:38.641 --> 00:03:41.642
"Pollyanna, how could you do this to me?

49
00:03:42.063 --> 00:03:46.345
You dressed me up, and then Aunt Polly shook her head in horror.

50
00:03:46.365 --> 00:03:49.247
"Let me be seen!"

51
00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:53.869
"But you looked perfectly lovely, Aunt Polly."

52
00:03:53.889 --> 00:03:57.972
"Lovely!" Aunt Polly said scornfully.

53
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.742
She flung the shawl aside and attacked her hair with shaking fingers.

54
00:04:02.762 --> 00:04:06.465
"Oh, Aunt Polly, please let your hair stay!"

55
00:04:10.587 --> 00:04:15.690
not!" Aunt Polly pulled her hair back so tightly that not a single curl remained.

56
00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:20.673
"But you looked so pretty!"

57
00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:24.556
Pollyanna was almost sobbing as she left the room.

58
00:04:27.688 --> 00:04:29.230
She went outside, where Dr.

59
00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.691
Chilton was waiting in his carriage.

60
00:04:30.711 --> 00:04:34.955
"Mr. Pendleton would like to see you now," he said.

61
00:04:34.975 --> 00:04:36.596
"Can you come with me?"

62
00:04:38.458 --> 00:04:39.960
Pollyanna was suddenly cheered up.

63
00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.522
"Let me ask Aunt Polly."

64
00:04:45.505 --> 00:04:47.867
She returned a few moments later, looking serious.

65
00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.289
"What's the matter?"

66
00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.952
Dr. Chilton asked as Pollyanna climbed in.

67
00:04:54.172 --> 00:04:57.834
"Aunt Polly doesn't want anything to do with me right now."

68
00:04:59.115 --> 00:05:00.236
The doctor hesitated.

69
00:05:00.256 --> 00:05:04.298
"Was that your aunt I saw with you at the window?"

70
00:05:05.999 --> 00:05:08.160
Pollyanna nodded and took a deep breath.

71
00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.862
"That's the whole trouble.

72
00:05:15.225 --> 00:05:17.946
I fixed her hair, and she looked so pretty.

73
00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:20.488
Didn't you think she looked lovely?"

74
00:05:22.156 --> 00:05:25.978
The doctor replied so quietly that Pollyanna could barely hear him.

75
00:05:25.998 --> 00:05:29.859
"Yes, I thought she looked lovely."

76
00:05:29.879 --> 00:05:32.380
"Oh, I'm glad!"

77
00:05:33.661 --> 00:05:35.181
Pollyanna looked happy again.

78
00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:37.482
"I'll be sure to tell her."

79
00:05:37.502 --> 00:05:41.964
"No!" To Pollyanna's alarm, Dr.

80
00:05:41.984 --> 00:05:43.284
Chilton was almost shouting.

81
00:05:43.304 --> 00:05:45.085
"Don't ever tell her that!"

82
00:05:45.105 --> 00:05:51.788
"Why? I'd think you'd be glad—" "But she might not be."
